# Server-side configuration. Copy to .env.local, which is gitignored.
#
#   cp server/.env.local.example server/.env.local
#
# Nothing in here is bundled or sent to a browser. That is the whole
# distinction: anything the client needs lives in client/.env.local with a
# VITE_ prefix and is public by construction, and anything with a VITE_ prefix
# is public whether you meant it to be or not. If a value would do damage in
# the hands of a visitor, it belongs in this file and never in that one.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Secrets
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Optional. Enables the JSearch source, which is the licensed route to LinkedIn,
# Indeed and Glassdoor postings. Without it that source fetches nothing and the
# sweep carries on; it is the one source reporting "0 fetched" today.
# Get one at rapidapi.com. Also set as a GitHub Actions secret so the CI sweep
# has it, or JSearch is only ever populated from your machine.
RAPIDAPI_KEY=

# Needed once the resume fit assessment ships. It must never reach the browser:
# an Anthropic key is billable, so exposing it means someone else spending your
# money. The assessment therefore runs in a serverless function under api/,
# which reads this from the Vercel dashboard in production rather than a file.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Almost certainly NOT needed, and listed so it is clear why.
#
# Supabase's sb_secret_ key bypasses row-level security entirely: it is full
# admin access to every user's data. Signed-in users act through their own
# session token instead, and the policies in supabase/migrations/0001_init.sql
# scope them to their own rows, which covers profiles, resumes and matches.
# Only reach for this if something has to act across users with no session at
# all. If you do set it, keep it here — never with a VITE_ prefix.
# SUPABASE_SECRET_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Not secrets, just configuration
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Where the sweep writes the job archive and companies.json. Must be a persistent
# path in a deployment, or the 30-day archive and the discovered company
# registry reset on every restart and the compounding effect is lost.
# DATA_DIR=./data

# Port for the local dev API server.
# PORT=4000

# Which repo and branch the serverless functions read sweep output from.
# Only needed if you fork: they default to the upstream data branch.
# DATA_REPO=Akius1/jobradar
# DATA_BRANCH=data

# How long the employer-careers-page prober waits before giving up.
# CAREERS_TIMEOUT_MS=6000
